<title>UK: UK's Clarke ups some National Insurance thresholds.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke ups some National Insurance thresholds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said he would raise the upper and lower earnings thresholds for employers' and employees' National Insurance contributions in his annual budget for 1997/8.</p>
<p>&quot;In this budget I propose to keep the three intermediate thresholds for employers' National Insurance Contributions where they are now,&quot; Clarke told Parliament.</p>
<p>&quot;I propose to increase, by 10 stg and one stg respectively, the upper and lower earnings thresholds for employers' and employees' National Insurance Contributions,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
